# React Runtime - Browser Hot Path

## Status

Admin UI tree is reset (`ui.mdc`). This file applies **after** milestone `admin_shell` when `web/src/pages` and `web/src/ui` exist again.

## Purpose

Apply when changing admin UI render loops: data grids, filters, charts, tickers, context providers, or fetch-driven list pages.

Maps tracker hot-path discipline (`hot-path.mdc`) to **V8 + React 19** in the browser. Layout and composition: `ui.mdc`.

## Runtime model (V8)

V8 uses a **generational garbage collector** (Orinoco): most objects die in the young generation (nursery). A **minor GC** (Scavenge) copies survivors to old space. **Major GC** (mark-compact, mostly concurrent) reclaims old space when heuristics fire.

| Fact | Implication for UI code |
| :--- | :--- |
| Allocation rate drives GC pauses | Fewer short-lived objects per frame = fewer jank spikes |
| No manual free | Reuse references, precompute, isolate churn - you cannot `free()` |
| Objects have **hidden classes** (maps) | Stable property order on repeated object shapes; avoid `delete obj.k`, avoid mixing arbitrary keys on hot DTOs |
| Strings are immutable (ECMA-262) | Each concat / template / `slice` may allocate; format once in `useMemo` |
| `Array.prototype.map/filter/flatMap` allocate new arrays (ECMA-262) | One pass in `useMemo`, not per-row chains in render |

There is no `GOGC` knob in the browser. The lever is **allocation rate** and **retained graph size** (closures, listeners, detached DOM).

## Interaction budgets (admin UI)

| Surface | Target | Knob |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Keystroke filter | Input to visible row update | < 50 ms perceived; debounce 150-300 ms for server refetch |
| Data grid scroll | Frame time during scroll | < 16 ms/frame (60 Hz); window rows, no layout read in scroll handler |
| Sort / page change | Full re-render of visible window | Pre-sorted array in `useMemo`; stable row keys |
| 1 Hz ticker (refresh countdown) | Must not re-render whole page | Isolated leaf component + `memo`; state colocated in ticker only |
| Chart resize/update | Avoid full React tree | Imperative uPlot/ECharts mount; React owns container only |

Cold admin path tolerates more allocation than tracker ingest, but **list pages with 500+ rows** follow hot rules below.

## Hot render path (forbidden)

Applies inside `rows.map`, scroll handlers, filter input handlers, and chart animation ticks.

| Category | Forbidden |
| :--- | :--- |
| Alloc per row | `rows.map(r => ({ ...r, label: format(r) }))` - format in precomputed parallel array or `Map` |
| O(n^2) | `.find` / `.filter` / `.some` inside row/cell render; nested `map` over full dataset per visible row |
| Fresh objects | Inline `style={{}}`, `className={cn(a, cond && b)}` with new object args every row unless `cn` is string-only |
| Fresh functions | Inline `onClick={() => ...}` on every row when child is `memo` - use row id + stable handler + lookup |
| JSON | `JSON.parse` / `JSON.stringify` in render |
| Sort/filter | `sortRows` / `applyFilters` in render body without `useMemo` |
| Context broadcast | Putting 1 Hz `now` or scroll offset in page-level context |
| Intervals | `setInterval` on page root updating shared parent state |
| DOM retention | Listeners on `document` without cleanup; closures over full `items[]` in listener |
| Spread chains | `[...a, ...b]`, `{...prev, ...patch}` in reducer every keystroke on large state |

## Allowed patterns

| Pattern | Usage |
| :--- | :--- |
| Snapshot state | Fetch result stored once; derive view in `useMemo` (sort, filter, page slice) |
| `Map` / `Set` indexes | `disputeIds`, `selectedIds`, `rowById` built in `useMemo` when parent data changes |
| Colocated state | Ticker, dropdown open, hover: state in leaf component; parent gets callbacks only |
| `useRef` | Mutable latest value (generation id, abort controller, previous width) without re-render |
| `memo` + stable props | Row cell components when row count > ~50 visible |
| `useCallback` | Only when passed to `memo` children or listed in effect deps on hot paths |
| `useMemo` | Sort/filter/slice/format lists; column defs; option lists for `Select` |
| Debounce / `requestAnimationFrame` | Search -> filter: debounce; scroll sync: rAF coalesce |
| Abort + generation | `useResource`: generation counter; ignore stale responses; `finally` clears `fetching` |
| Imperative charts | `echarts_mount.ts` / uPlot: update series in place; React does not re-render series arrays each tick |
| `WeakMap` | Cache keyed by row object identity when same row instances preserved across updates |

## State shape (how to store)

Follow **cold snapshot + derived view**, same spirit as `atomic.Pointer` catalog swap in Go.

```
Server snapshot (useState / useResource data)
    -> useMemo: filteredRows
    -> useMemo: sortedRows
    -> useMemo: pageRows = slice(sortedRows, page * size, ...)
    -> render: pageRows.map(Row)
```

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| One source of truth | API DTO in `data`; UI toggles (sort key, page, filters) in separate primitive state |
| Draft vs applied | Filter panel: draft in local state; apply copies to applied filters (one object write) |
| Minimal lift | Lift only what siblings must share; dropdown open state stays in dropdown |
| Reducer size | Reducer state: plain fields; avoid deep clone of 500-row arrays on each keypress |
| URL sync | Serialize filter/page to search params in effect or on Apply - not on every keystroke |
| Error | `error` string or `ServiceError` object stored once; render branches explicit (`ui.mdc`) |

Forbidden state shapes:

- Single giant `useState({ rows, sort, filter, ui, ... })` updated with spread each keystroke
- Duplicated row arrays (`items` + `displayItems` + `sortedItems` all copies in state)
- Storing formatted strings in state when format can run in `useMemo` from primitives

## Data-oriented lists (SoA in JS)

For directories (customers, campaigns, audit):

| AoS (avoid hot) | SoA / index (prefer) |
| :--- | :--- |
| Row component reads 12 fields from object and formats inline | `useMemo` builds `balanceDisplay[i]` parallel to `rows` or `Map<id, display>` |
| Filter scans all rows per render | `useMemo` filtered list; optional inverted index for text search if needed |
| Selection: `selectedIds.includes(id)` per row O(n) | `Set` in `useMemo` |

Row component receives **primitives or preformatted strings**, not whole DTO plus formatters.

## Closures and retention (heap leaks)

V8 keeps objects reachable from roots: global, closures, DOM wrappers, compile caches.

| Leak pattern | Fix |
| :--- | :--- |
| `useEffect(() => { const t = setInterval(...); }, [])` without cleanup | `return () => clearInterval(t)` |
| `document.addEventListener` in effect | Remove in cleanup; use `{ capture, passive }` intentionally |
| Async `fetch` after unmount | `AbortController`; generation id check before `setState` |
| Closure over `items` in interval | Store `itemsRef.current = items`; interval reads ref |
| Detached DOM | Portal menus: unmount on close; do not `display:none` huge subtrees with listeners |
| Global module cache unbounded | Cap LRU or `WeakMap`; never `Map` all rows forever in module scope |

ECMAScript `WeakRef` / `FinalizationRegistry`: use only for optional caches; do not rely on them for correctness.

## Effects and subscriptions

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Effect scope | One concern per effect (fetch, subscribe, sync URL) |
| Deps | Minimal deps; refs for values that must not retrigger effect |
| Strict Mode | Effects mount twice in dev; cleanup must be idempotent |
| Fetch | `useResource` or explicit effect with abort; no fetch in render |
| Subscriptions | Websocket/poll: single effect; push into snapshot state, not per-event spread of full list |

## React reconciliation (minimize work)

React re-renders when state or context changes on that subtree.

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Split trees | Page sections as siblings; ticker state does not live in page parent |
| Context split | Separate contexts for auth vs theme vs data; narrow consumers |
| `key` | Stable `row.id`; never index-only for reorderable/sorted lists |
| `memo` | Row/cell when parent re-renders often (ticker, layout) but row props unchanged |
| Children as props | Avoid `children={<Heavy />}` recreated inline when parent is hot |

React Compiler (if enabled later): still follow allocation rules; compiler does not remove GC pressure from new arrays.

## V8-friendly object habits

| Habit | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Stable option lists | `const STATUS_OPTIONS = [...]` module scope; not recreated in component body |
| `as const` tuples | Column defs and label maps at module scope |
| Avoid `delete` | Omit keys when building new object; do not mutate shape of cached DTO |
| Number / string keys | Record maps: `Record<string, T>` built once; not `switch` with closure per case in loop |
| `cn()` | String class names only in row loop; no object form in hot list |

## Charts and canvas

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Ownership | React: container `div` + resize observer; chart lib owns series buffers |
| Update | `setOption` / `setData` in place; do not pass new React element tree per point |
| Unmount | `dispose()` chart instance in effect cleanup |
| Resize | rAF-debounced resize; read `getBoundingClientRect` once per frame max |

## Verification

| Step | Command / tool |
| :--- | :--- |
| Types | `cd web && npm run typecheck` |
| UI gates | `bash scripts/ci/check_ui_surface_gate.sh` && `bash scripts/ci/admin_web.sh` |
| React Profiler | Record filter typing + sort on 500-row fixture; commit count should not include full page for 1 Hz ticker |
| Performance panel | Chrome: 6x slowdown; watch **Scripting** and **GC** during scroll |
| Memory | Heap snapshot before/after 10 navigate cycles; detached nodes and listener count stable |
| Allocation instrumentation | DevTools > Memory > Allocation sampling on `customers_page` filter: spike only on apply, not per key |

Before claiming list perf: paste Profiler screenshot or note visible row window size and row count.

